>> title: Pulled Roast Chicken
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, roast, make-ahead, bowl, meal prep
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: pulled chicken, hand-pulled chicken, shredded roast chicken, rotisserie-style chicken, plain roast chicken, chicken for bowls
>> pairs-with: mujaddara, tahini-sauce, basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 6
>> time: 13 hr
>> slack: narrow — the thighs come off at 175°F; pulled short of that the connective tissue has not melted and the meat will not shred
>> step.1: salt uncovered in the fridge 12 hr
>> step.2: roast 425°F (220°C) 35 min, skin up
>> step.3: rest 15 min in the pan
>> step.4: shred it back into its own juices

Salt @boneless chicken thighs{2%lb}(900 g; skin on) with @kosher salt{2%tsp} and leave them on a rack, uncovered, in the fridge ~chill{12%hr}.

Rub @&(~1)salted thighs{} with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and ~roast{35%min} skin up on a #sheet pan{} at 425°F (220°C), until the skin is the colour of a walnut and the thickest thigh reads 175°F (80°C).

Leave @&(~1)roasted thighs{} to ~rest{15%min} in the pan.

Pull @&(~1)rested chicken{} apart with two forks **in the pan**, working the shreds through @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @extra-virgin olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and the fat and juice already there.
